    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "### Motivation\n- Reframe the repository as a governed, research-only system for discovering and evaluating speculative signal hypotheses with strong safety boundaries.\n- Prevent any automation from introducing live-trading logic and require human approval for all strategy-affecting changes.\n- Provide auditable, machine-generated improvement proposals and governance state to close the feedback → proposal → validation loop.\n- Standardize artifacts (schemas, registries, scorecards) so simulations and review outputs are structured and reproducible.\n\n### Description\n- Add CI workflows to support the loop: `feedback-ingest.yml`, `draft-pr-generator.yml`, `governance.yml`, `simulation-validation.yml`, `repo-self-review.yml`, and `weekly-evolution-report.yml` with guardrails to keep PRs draft and block auto-merge. \n- Introduce ingestion/governor tooling: `scripts/feedback_classifier.py`, `scripts/proposal_writer.py`, and `scripts/llm_governor.py` to normalize feedback, generate proposal JSON, and build governance state. \n- Add schemas and example artifacts for machine-readable proposals and candidate signals: `improvement_proposals/schema.json`, `candidate_signal_registry/schema.json`, example JSONs, and `cache/governance_state.json`. \n- Expand documentation, safety policies, and repo structure with a new `README.md`, `docs/REPO_REDESIGN_PLAN.md`, `docs/SIGNAL_DISCOVERY_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `safety_policies/RESEARCH_GUARDRAILS.md`, scoring rubric, change summaries, and placeholders for review artifacts. \n\n### Testing\n- No automated CI jobs were executed as part of this PR; the change adds CI jobs that will run on the next workflow triggers. \n- The new workflows include automated checks such as `python -m compileall scripts` and a safety file existence check `test -f safety_policies/RESEARCH_GUARDRAILS.md` which will run in CI. \n- `feedback-ingest` is configured to run `python scripts/feedback_classifier.py` and `python scripts/proposal_writer.py`, and `governance` is configured to run `python scripts/llm_governor.py` during scheduled or triggered runs. \n- `simulation-validation` will perform compile checks and emit a placeholder `simulation_runs/last_validation.json` as part of its validation job.\n\n------\n[Codex Task](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/tasks/task_e_69e07c7dc1cc8321a89daeedae2bf410)",
